      "title": "Affordable Care Act market reforms",
      "narration": "The ACA rewrote the rules for comprehensive medical coverage. Individual health insurance coverage means coverage sold to individuals in the individual market, as opposed to group plans. Plans must cover children on a parent’s policy to age 26. They may not impose lifetime dollar limits, or annual dollar limits, on essential health benefits, the ten categories every individual and small group plan must include. Premiums may vary only by age, within a 3 to 1 ratio, tobacco use up to 1.5 to 1, geographic area and family size. Group plans may not impose waiting periods longer than 90 days.",
