      "title": "COBRA and Maryland continuation differ",
      "text": "COBRA is federal and applies to larger employers. Maryland’s own continuation statutes reach group contracts of any size and give 18 months after a loss of employment not for cause, after the death of the insured, or after divorce, with a 45-day election. Lesson 38 compares them.",
